 4. 🏛️ McConnell&#x27;s Capitol comeback 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Allison Robbert/AP Sen. Mitch McConnell (R-Ky.) voted at the Capitol yesterday for the first time in three months after being hospitalized in June, Axios' Stef W. Kight and Avery Lotz write. 

 McConnell arrived in a wheelchair and spoke briefly to reporters, joking that after years of avoiding their questions, he "wasn't sure how many of you would be here today. But I'm glad to see you. It's time to get back to work." McConnell said he 's ready to work on the farm bill, and on supporting NATO and Ukraine.

