 5. ⚠️ Charted: The AI fear trade 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep . Chart: Emily Peck/Axios Fear is splitting the AI trade: The same advances that are raising alarms about rogue agents, cyberattacks and apocalypse are creating a bull case for the companies paid to protect against those threats, Axios' Emily Peck writes. 

 Calls for a slowdown in the advancement of the most sophisticated models pushed down stocks in sectors connected to the AI trade, like chip and memory companies. At the same time, stocks rose for cybersecurity companies. CrowdStrike and Palo Alto Networks — two of the industry's largest companies — were up yesterday roughly 14% and 13%, respectively. Get Axios Markets . 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 6. ⛽ &quot;Great Fuel Crisis&quot; arrives 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images The prolonged disruption of the Strait of Hormuz has triggered the fuel crisis that oil executives have been warning about for months, The Wall Street Journal reports . 

 "Commercial fuel stocks around the world have been depleting for more than six months, and strategic crude reserves can't be tapped much further," the paper says. Today's national average gas price is $4.33 for a gallon of regular. Between the lines: 49 days before the midterms, it's hard to see a scenario where prices come down quickly.

